  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Binomial Expansions: Pascal's triangle</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 1.2: Write down the row of Pascal's triangle for power n (6 to 10), and either its sum or the sum of the coefficients of (1 + 2x)^n.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 5, Section A, question A2(b) of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 2 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2004: extended from the next row to the row for a power from 6 to 10, randomised, with the row sum or the sum of the coefficients of (1 + 2x)^n added.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
